{"code":"29-1124.00","title":"Radiation Therapists","description":"Provide radiation therapy to patients as prescribed by a radiation oncologist according to established practices and standards. Duties may include reviewing prescription and diagnosis; acting as liaison with physician and supportive care personnel; preparing equipment, such as immobilization, treatment, and protection devices; and maintaining records, reports, and files. May assist in dosimetry procedures and tumor localization.","jobZone":3,"kinds":{"R":{"score":4.96,"share":0.2505},"I":{"score":4.64,"share":0.2302},"A":{"score":1.24,"share":0.0152},"S":{"score":4.77,"share":0.2385},"E":{"score":1.72,"share":0.0455},"C":{"score":4.48,"share":0.2201}},"highPoints":["R","S","I"],"tasks":[{"id":4085,"text":"Administer prescribed doses of radiation to specific body parts, using radiation therapy equipment according to established practices and standards.","core":true,"importance":4.89,"relevance":93.72,"frequency":6.42},{"id":4086,"text":"Position patients for treatment with accuracy, according to prescription.","core":true,"importance":4.89,"relevance":98.04,"frequency":6.47},{"id":4088,"text":"Follow principles of radiation protection for patient, self, and others.","core":true,"importance":4.85,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.41},{"id":4090,"text":"Review prescription, diagnosis, patient chart, and identification.","core":true,"importance":4.82,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.28},{"id":4091,"text":"Conduct most treatment sessions independently, in accordance with the long-term treatment plan and under the general direction of the patient's physician.","core":true,"importance":4.8,"relevance":89.37,"frequency":5.99},{"id":4087,"text":"Enter data into computer and set controls to operate or adjust equipment or regulate dosage.","core":true,"importance":4.78,"relevance":90.18,"frequency":6.21},{"id":4092,"text":"Check radiation therapy equipment to ensure proper operation.","core":true,"importance":4.74,"relevance":96.79,"frequency":5.15},{"id":4093,"text":"Observe and reassure patients during treatment and report unusual reactions to physician or turn equipment off if unexpected adverse reactions occur.","core":true,"importance":4.69,"relevance":97.59,"frequency":5.94},{"id":4095,"text":"Educate, prepare, and reassure patients and their families by answering questions, providing physical assistance, and reinforcing physicians' advice regarding treatment reactions or post-treatment care.","core":true,"importance":4.64,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.67},{"id":4089,"text":"Maintain records, reports, or files as required, including such information as radiation dosages, equipment settings, or patients' reactions.","core":true,"importance":4.63,"relevance":98.03,"frequency":6.03},{"id":4094,"text":"Check for side effects, such as skin irritation, nausea, or hair loss to assess patients' reaction to treatment.","core":true,"importance":4.56,"relevance":92.84,"frequency":6.04},{"id":4097,"text":"Prepare or construct equipment, such as immobilization, treatment, or protection devices.","core":true,"importance":4.54,"relevance":92.51,"frequency":5},{"id":4099,"text":"Help physicians, radiation oncologists, or clinical physicists to prepare physical or technical aspects of radiation treatment plans, using information about patient condition and anatomy.","core":true,"importance":4.48,"relevance":83.57,"frequency":4.68},{"id":4096,"text":"Calculate actual treatment dosages delivered during each session.","core":true,"importance":4.46,"relevance":69.88,"frequency":3.84},{"id":4098,"text":"Photograph treated area of patient and process film.","core":true,"importance":4.43,"relevance":97.32,"frequency":5.59},{"id":4101,"text":"Act as liaison with physicist and supportive care personnel.","core":true,"importance":4.43,"relevance":88.26,"frequency":5.49},{"id":4103,"text":"Implement appropriate follow-up care plans.","core":false,"importance":4.2,"relevance":64.17,"frequency":4.73},{